Package: birt
Type: Package
Title: BIvariate Response Time Modeling with 'lavaan'-Style Syntax
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com")
Description: Fits item response theory models with one or two latent variables, for
    example ability and speed in joint models of response accuracy and response time
    (van der Linden, 2007, <doi:10.1007/s11336-006-1478-z>), from 'lavaan'-style model
    syntax. The main engine fits the syntax in 'RTMB' by approximate Bayesian inference as an
    extended latent Gaussian model (Stringer, Brown and Stafford, 2023,
    <doi:10.1080/10618600.2022.2099403>): the persons are integrated out by adaptive
    Gauss-Hermite quadrature and the remaining parameters by an outer adaptive quadrature, with
    marginal likelihoods for model comparison; the same engine gives maximum likelihood, with
    casewise scores for score-based invariance tests and DIF trees. Ordinal and continuous
    indicators, moderated nonlinear factor analysis statements, sinh-arcsinh residuals (Jones
    and Pewsey, 2009, <doi:10.1093/biomet/asp053>) whose quantile effects at every level come
    from one fit, conditional reliability and the information of each quantile regression of
    the response times.
    An optional 'JAGS' engine translates the model into a plain 'JAGS' model file, for
    spike-and-slab priors and asymmetric Laplace (quantile) distributions, with
    marginal-likelihood fit indices (DIC, WAIC, PSIS-LOO) and posterior predictive checks.
